                "text": "**Analyzing Input Dimensions**\n\nI'm currently focused on the input grid dimensions across different training runs. It looks like the output width is always exactly half of the input width, while the height remains the same. I'm investigating if there's always a consistent relationship between these sizes.\n\n\n**Investigating Data Division**\n\nI've discovered the input grid is split into Left and Right halves. It seems the output always adopts the background color of either the Left or Right side. I'm focusing on why Train 2 chose the Right side, while the other runs selected the Left. I've noticed shapes on the Right side get pasted onto the Left. Now, I'm examining if this is consistent. I think the shape is used as a template!\n\n\n**Uncovering Alignment Mechanisms**\n\nI've made a breakthrough. I realized the output is formed by pasting shapes from the right side onto the left side based on matching values. The '6' on the right was placed onto the '6' on the left. Furthermore, after going back to train 1, it became clear: the 1's on the right are pasted onto the 1's on the left. The output is a paste of the full shape from right, aligned to the matching pixels on the left. I think this explains a lot!\n\n\n",
